{"book":6,"chapter":20,"context":{"chapter":20,"title":"Six Cities of Refuge","summary":"God tells Joshua to set apart cities of refuge where someone who killed by accident can be safe until trial. Three are named west of the Jordan and three east.","background":"Moses had commanded these cities (Numbers 35; Deuteronomy 19). The six were spread across the land so no one was too far from safety: Kedesh in the north, Shechem in the center, Hebron in the south, and Bezer, Ramoth and Golan in the east. All six were also Levite towns (ch. 21).","customs":[{"term":"Stating the case at the gate","verses":"20:4","note":"The fugitive explained his case to the city's elders at the gate, where public business and trials took place."},{"term":"Until the high priest's death","verses":"20:6","note":"The manslayer could go home only after the high priest died. The reason is not explained; many see the high priest's death as closing the matter."}],"watchFor":["'Unawares and unwittingly' (vv. 3, 5) marks the difference between accident and murder.","The cities protect foreigners as well as Israelites (v. 9)."],"connections":["Exodus 21:12-13","Numbers 35:25-28","Deuteronomy 19:1-10","Hebrews 6:18"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְדַבֵּר","vaydaber","H1696","Hc/Vpw3ms","and he spoke"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["יְהוֹשֻׁעַ","yehoshua'","H3091","HNpm","Joshua"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"]]},"2":{"w":[["דַּבֵּר","daber","H1696","HVpv2ms","speak"],["אֶל","'el-","H413","HR","to"],["בְּנֵי","benei","H1121","HNcmpc","[the] people of"],["יִשְׂרָאֵל","yisra'el","H3478","HNpl","Israel"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"],["תְּנוּ","tenu","H5414","HVqv2mp","assign"],["לָכֶם","lakhem","H9036","HRd/Sp2mp","for <the> yourselves"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["עָרֵי","'arei","H5892","HNcmpc","[the] cities of"],["הַמִּקְלָט","hamiklat","H4733","HTd/Ncmsa","<the> refuge"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher-","H834","HTr","whic